A program teq compiles for JavaScript or runs in its interpreter carries the parts of teq's standard library it
uses, which may include the adaptations from Scala.js, the Scala standard library, scalajs-dom and
scala-java-locales named below and the character tables made from the Unicode Character Database; a build with
--hot carries the react-refresh runtime. Those entries' notices accompany a distribution of a program that
contains them. The entries for the test programs, the rules of `teq fix`, the Zed extension's files, the
compiler's hash algorithm and the Rust crates linked into teq's binary concern teq itself, not the programs it
compiles.

